## How a pattern is written

| Part | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Problem frame** | The situation the pattern fits; check it before applying. |
| **Solution** | The working moves the pattern prescribes. |
| **Worked case** | A constructed example showing the pattern in use. |
| **Conformance checklist** | Items to inspect your own result against. |
| **Relations** | Other patterns that supply an input or receive the result. |

A pattern body ends at its `:End` heading. Section references such as
`SYSE.24:4.1` point inside the body; read through to the next heading of the
same or a higher level.

